  "overall_paraphrase": "On the strongest available reading, this segment is most likely an extract from a epicurean ethical prose (philodemus tradition). The recurring vocabulary, the script style, and the column layout all point in that direction; the actual text on the surface, however, is too fragmentary to recover continuously, and the reading should be treated as a weighted hypothesis rather than a transcription.",
  "interpretation": [
    "This segment (20231106155351) preserves 72 letter positions across 6 strips. The most-anchored letters are Μ Ι Α Τ Ε Ο, distributed roughly evenly through the column. Mean per-letter confidence is 0.27, placing the segment in the 'speculative' band: anchors can be cited individually, but a continuous transcription is not yet defensible.",
